## The Architecture

Status vaporizes at 42°C. The CEO soaks beside the delivery driver, both temporarily stripped to essential humanity. In our stratified world, this fleeting equality feels revolutionary.

## The Hypothesis

Japan doesn't oppose tradition against innovation—it layers them thoughtfully. Onsen isn't merely a longevity ingredient but a metaphor: intentional immersion, strategic withdrawal, and mindful oscillation between extremes.

MIT taught me algorithms and optimization; onsen taught me their limits. Bruce Lee said "Be water, my friend"—adaptable, formless, flowing. But in these volcanic waters, I've learned to strive for more: be my friend, water.

The engineer seeks to master the elements; the onsen teaches us to be mastered by them instead.
